From: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:29:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Use local tracking refs in Git URL tests

The URL-selection tests only inspect branch tracking configuration.
Creating the remote-tracking ref from HEAD supplies that configuration
without fetching GitHub in the offline build environment.

Upstream: https://github.com/docker/buildx/blob/v0.38.0/util/gitutil/gittestutil/testutil.go
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [offline distribution builds]
Signed-off-by: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
--- a/util/gitutil/gittestutil/testutil.go
+++ b/util/gitutil/gittestutil/testutil.go
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@
 
 func GitSetMainUpstream(c *gitutil.GitCLI, tb testing.TB, remote, target string) {
 	tb.Helper()
-	_, err := fakeGit(c, "fetch", "--depth", "1", remote, target)
+	_, err := fakeGit(c, "update-ref", "refs/remotes/"+remote+"/"+target, "HEAD")
 	require.NoError(tb, err)
 
 	_, err = fakeGit(c, "branch", "--set-upstream-to", remote+"/"+target, "main")
